  era: "Section 15 \xB7 Bhakti and Sufi Movements \xB7 c. 6th \u2013 17th century"
  title: Kabir
  text: Kabir, a 15th-century weaver of Varanasi, rejected ritual and caste in both Hinduism and Islam and praised a formless God. His sharp couplets, or dohas, are in everyday Hindi, and some appear in the Guru Granth Sahib.
